# 252-APP-0026 — The VITS voices in `mind::nn`: Piper and Vosk TTS 0.7 give onnxruntime's audio — done

**Type:** tools (voice) · **Owner:** tools track (`APP`) · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-10-09) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** [252](../issues/252-neural-speech-synthesis.md) (step 4, VITS) · **Roadmap:** track G · **Constitution:** MC-12.1, MC-12.2

## Problem

Two of the chosen voices are VITS:

- the compact Russian voice, Vosk TTS 0.7;
- the English Piper voices.

Both are ONNX graphs. A text encoder, a duration predictor, a flow and a HiFi-GAN decoder (an iSTFT head in Vosk TTS) run in one graph. The dictation work left an interpreter of the operators the speech recognizers use ([250-APP-0021](250-APP-0021-network-interpreter.done) to [0025](250-APP-0025-dictate-in-the-system.done)).

Converting Piper's `en_US-lessac-high` showed what was missing:

- string attributes (`Pad`'s mode);
- sixteen operators.

## Plan

- **The network file:** attributes of kind 6, a string (its UTF-8 bytes). `convert.py` writes them and `mind::nn` reads them (`Node::text`).
- **Operators** (`libmind/src/nn/extra.rs`, the rest in `ops.rs`, opset 15):
  - `Pad`: constant (row by row), reflect, edge; negative pads cut.
  - `Split`: given sizes, or equal parts.
  - `Less`, `LessOrEqual`, `And`, `Or`, `Xor`, `Not`.
  - `NonZero`, `GatherND`, `CumSum` (exclusive, reverse).
  - `LeakyRelu`, `Erf` (series below 2, else erfc's continued fraction, about 1e-15), `Softplus` (as onnxruntime computes it), `Sqrt`, `Ceil`, `Floor`.
  - `RandomNormalLike`: Box–Muller over xorshift with a fixed seed, so a voice says a sentence the same way each time.
  - `ConvTranspose` in one dimension: one product x^T·w per group, then col2im.
- **Speed** (the HiFi-GAN decoder is nearly all of the time):
  - im2col copies whole runs of an input row instead of one element at a time;
  - blocks of at least 256 columns, up to 4 MiB;
  - the f32 product packs each 256×16 block of B into one run, blocks k by 256, and has 4- and 2-row kernels for the rows left over.
- **The comparison:**
  - `scripts/voice_tts/vits_reference.py` makes onnxruntime's audio with the noise scales at 0, and optionally every value.
  - Piper's phonemes come through piper-phonemize (espeak-ng, GPL-3.0, on the host only); Vosk TTS's come from vosk-tts.
  - `vits_against_onnxruntime` in `tests/nn_host.rs` compares the audio and, with a dump, finds the first value that departs.

## Acceptance criteria

- **CI** (`tests/nn_host.rs`, `tests/fbank_host.rs`):
  - every new operator against values worked out by hand;
  - `ConvTranspose` against its definition, with strides, padding, dilation and groups;
  - `Erf` to 1e-14;
  - a convolution whose padding is wider than its input.
- **By hand:** the audio of both voices equals onnxruntime's within 1e-3 of its peak.

## Resolution

- **Measured on this host** (one thread, AVX2, a shared Xeon):

  | Voice | Sentence | Audio | Largest difference (of peak) | SNR | Time | onnxruntime, one thread (252) |
  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
  | Piper `en_US-lessac-high` (114 MB, fp32) | "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog." | 2.50 s | 4.1·10⁻⁵ (of 0.70) | 92.6 dB | 3.0–3.8 s | 0.73 of real time |
  | Vosk TTS 0.7, speaker 3 (146 MB) | «Привет! Это проверка русского синтеза речи в системе.» | 3.44 s | 5.5·10⁻⁵ (of 0.47) | 89.6 dB | 1.0 s | 0.06 of real time |

  Only the random noise differs from onnxruntime's values, and it is multiplied by 0 here.
- **Where the time goes:**
  - The decoder's convolutions take 80 % of the time; the products there reach 21–36 GMAC/s with AVX2.
  - onnxruntime is faster on this host. MLAS convolves with AVX-512 here, and our AVX2 code runs at half its peak.
  - The two models are not equal in cost: Piper "high" upsamples to the sample rate through four HiFi-GAN stages, while Vosk TTS ends in an iSTFT.
- **Code:**
  - [`libmind/src/nn/extra.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/extra.rs) (new), [`ops.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/ops.rs), [`gemm.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/gemm.rs), [`mod.rs`](../libmind/src/nn/mod.rs);
  - [`libmind/src/voice/math.rs`](../libmind/src/voice/math.rs);
  - [`scripts/voice_dictate/convert.py`](../scripts/voice_dictate/convert.py), [`scripts/voice_tts/vits_reference.py`](../scripts/voice_tts/vits_reference.py).
- **Not done here:**
  - the phonemes in the system (step 3);
  - a voice speaking in the system (step 5);
  - AVX-512 and NEON products;
  - CER of our audio on the 24 sentences.

